# What NOT to ship inside the .vsix.
#
# Everything here is downloaded by every user who installs the extension, so the
# package holds the extension and the three files a marketplace listing is made of
# (README.md, CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE) - nothing else.

# Editor scaffolding
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.gitignore
.yarnrc
vsc-extension-quickstart.md

# Sources and build inputs. The compiled out/*.js is what runs; the TypeScript it
# was built from, its config and its linter rules are of no use to an installed
# copy. *.map is listed for the default (non---release) build, which emits them.
src/**
**/tsconfig.json
**/.eslintrc.json
**/*.map
**/*.ts
node_modules/**
out/test/**

# Build and install tooling. These operate ON this directory in a development
# checkout; inside an installed extension they are dead weight that also invites
# somebody to run them against the wrong tree.
build.sh
install.sh

# Internal development documentation. Written for people working on the RSpade
# framework, not for people using the extension - CLAUDE.md is agent instructions,
# and the rest document internals and setup of the monorepo. The user-facing
# documentation is README.md, which ships.
CLAUDE.md
SETUP.md
GOTO_DEFINITION.md
JQHTML_HIGHLIGHTING.md
